{"title":"Quadrilateral","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Types_of_quadrilaterals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Types of quadrilaterals</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Kite\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Kite</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Cyclic_Quadrilateral\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Cyclic Quadrilateral</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Parallelogram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Parallelogram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Rhombus\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rhombus</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Rectangle\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rectangle</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Square\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Square</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Introductory_topics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory topics</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Books\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Books</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Intermediate_topics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate topics</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Resources_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Books_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Books</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <b>quadrilateral</b> is a four-sided <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygon</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Types_of_quadrilaterals\">Types of quadrilaterals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Types of quadrilaterals\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Kite\">Kite</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Kite\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kite\" title=\"Kite\">Kite</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A kite is a quadrilateral with two pairs of adjacent <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruent\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Congruent\">congruent</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\">edges</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cyclic_Quadrilateral\">Cyclic Quadrilateral</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Cyclic Quadrilateral\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_quadrilateral\" title=\"Cyclic quadrilateral\">Cyclic quadrilateral</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A cyclic quadrilateral is a <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">quadrilateral</a> that is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic\" title=\"Cyclic\">cyclic</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Parallelogram\">Parallelogram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Parallelogram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelogram\" title=\"Parallelogram\">Parallelogram</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A parallelogram is a quadrilateral with two pairs of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\">edges</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rhombus\">Rhombus</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Rhombus\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rhombus\" title=\"Rhombus\">Rhombus</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A rhombus is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral\" title=\"Equilateral\">equilateral</a> parallelogram.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Rectangle\">Rectangle</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Rectangle\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">Rectangle</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A rectangle is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equiangular\" title=\"Equiangular\">equiangular</a> parallelogram.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Square\">Square</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Square\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)\" title=\"Square (geometry)\">Square (geometry)</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A square is any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Figure&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Figure (page does not exist)\">figure</a> that is both a rectangle and a rhombus.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory_topics\">Introductory topics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory topics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_quadrilateral\" title=\"Cyclic quadrilateral\">Cyclic quadrilaterals</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Books\">Books</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Books\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Books/AoPS_B_Item.php?page_id=9\">Introduction to Geometry</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Richard_Rusczyk\" title=\"Richard Rusczyk\">Richard Rusczyk</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate_topics\">Intermediate topics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate topics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s Theorem\">Ptolemy's Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Brahmagupta%27s_formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Brahmagupta&#39;s formula\">Brahmagupta's formula</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources_2\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Books_2\">Books</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Books\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0486691543/artofproblems-20\">Challenging Problems in Geometry</a> -- A good book for students who already have a solid handle on elementary geometry.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0883856190/artofproblems-20\">Geometry Revisited</a> -- A classic.</li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003320\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 121/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 720/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 248/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.012      1 -total\n 65.76%   11.188      6 Template:Main\n 31.04%    5.280      6 Template:Hatnote\n 29.31%    4.987      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1769:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003320 and revision id 240322. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}